 two waves are given by :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>These waves are simultaneously passing through a string. The amplitude of the resulting wave is :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d3d76e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67ab"}, {"id": "0e2574", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67ac"}, {"id": "9837f9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67ad"}, {"id": "dffe24", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67ae"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67af", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["6117b60b478ae845c43c641a"], "concepts": ["61adb634dec0c790740acc84"], "question": {"text": "A string is clamped at both the ends and it is vibrating in its <math><msup><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> harmonic. The equation of the stationary wave is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0.157</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>200</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. The length of the string is<br />(All quantities are in <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> units.)"}, "options": [{"id": "ef3be6", "text": "<math><mn>20</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67b0"}, {"id": "c935ad", "text": "<math><mn>60</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67b1"}, {"id": "c8630d", "text": "<math><mn>40</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67b2"}, {"id": "2bd452", "text": "<math><mn>80</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67b3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67b4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475b"], "concepts": ["6117b9b767dbe2603c3ea7c9"], "question": {"text": "A student is performing the experiment of the resonance column. The diameter of the column tube is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The frequency of the tuning fork is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>504</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. Speed of the sound at the given temperature is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>336</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The zero of the meter scale coincides with the top end of the resonance column tube. The reading of the water level in the column when the first resonance occurs is:"}, "options": [{"id": "e190d7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67b5"}, {"id": "6ef28a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67b6"}, {"id": "06fc8f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67b7"}, {"id": "b02427", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67b8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67b9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["6162fb156ed13040ec84ade8"], "concepts": ["6162fb176ed13040ec84aeb4"], "question": {"text": "The ratio of speed of sound in hydrogen gas to the speed of sound in oxygen gas at the same temperature is:"}, "options": [{"id": "1526f2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67ba"}, {"id": "ad3c03", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67bb"}, {"id": "d1a623", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67bc"}, {"id": "f2ee93", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67bd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67be", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e