 minima will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "bab76f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67d8"}, {"id": "45a351", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>81</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67d9"}, {"id": "bf6584", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>169</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67da"}, {"id": "3e3311", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67db"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67dc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475b"], "concepts": ["6117b64d478ae845c43c684a"], "question": {"text": "In an experiment with a closed organ pipe, it is filled with water by $\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)$ th of its volume. The frequency of the fundamental note will change by"}, "options": [{"id": "2b49ae", "text": "$25 \\%$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67dd"}, {"id": "5512b5", "text": "$20 \\%$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67de"}, {"id": "22c7e4", "text": "$-20 \\%$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67df"}, {"id": "8fc711", "text": "$-25 \\%$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67e0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67e1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["6162fb156ed13040ec84ade8"], "concepts": ["6162fb176ed13040ec84aeb2"], "question": {"text": "For a solid rod, the Young&#39;s modulus of elasticity is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and density is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The velocity of longitudinal wave in the rod will be"}, "options": [{"id": "b73f97", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>145</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67e2"}, {"id": "0d60d6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67e3"}, {"id": "393ee5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>96</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67e4"}, {"id": "a6e424", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67e5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67e6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e567ac499d1e49588f95ea"], "concepts": ["6176f3f16581241c7072ab38"], "question": {"text": "A radar sends an electromagnetic signal of electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> which strikes a target on line of sight at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> in a medium. After that, a part of signal (echo) reflects back towards the radar with same velocity and by same path. If the signal was transmitted at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;from radar, then after how much time echo will reach to the radar?"}, "options": [{"id": "490dfb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67e7"}, {"id": "0021fa", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67e8"}, {"id": "6e6426", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67e9"}, {"id": "620afa", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67ea"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67eb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e56769499d1e49588f8f08"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f993a"], "question": {"text": "A wire of length <math><mi>L</mi></math> and mass per unit length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6.0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is put under tension of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>540</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Two consecutive frequencies that it resonates at are: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>420</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>490</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Then <math><mi>L</mi></math> in meters is :"}, "options": [{"id": "0c9d04", "text": "<math><mn>2.1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67ec"}, {"id": "78f6ad", "text": "<math><mn>1.1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67ed"}, {"id": "213753", "text": "<math><mn>8.1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67ee"}, {"id": "737e2b", "text": "<math><mn>5.1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67ef"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67f0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475b"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba0"], "question": {"text": "The fundamental frequency of a closed organ pipe is equal to the first overtone frequency of an open organ pipe. If length of the open pipe is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, the length of the closed pipe will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "9b3885", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67f1"}, {"id": "c941b6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67f2"}, {"id": "8c39a3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67f3"}, {"id": "ecc172", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67f4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67f5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f38"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4efb"], "question": {"text": "<p>Match List I with List II</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><strong>List I</strong></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><strong>List II</strong></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>A</td>\t\t\t<td>Troposphere</td>\t\t\t<td>I</td>\t\t\t<td>Approximate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>65</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> over Earth&rsquo;s surface</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>B</td>\t\t\t<td>E-Part of Stratosphere</td>\t\t\t<td>II</td>\t\t\t<td>Approximate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> over Earth&rsquo;s surface</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>C</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>-Part of Thermosphere</td>\t\t\t<td>III</td>\t\t\t<td>Approximate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> over Earth&rsquo;s surface</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>D</td>\t\t\t<td>D-Part of Stratosphere</td>\t\t\t<td>IV</td>\t\t\t<td>Approximate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> over Earth&rsquo;s surface</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "bc8661", "text": "A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67f6"}, {"id": "8c7f86", "text": "A-I, B-II, C-IV, D-III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67f7"}, {"id": "6650a1", "text": "A-I, B-IV, C-III, D-II", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67f8"}, {"id": "1981a9", "text": "A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67f9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67fa", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e56769499d1e49588f8f06"], "concepts": ["62e0f4aa3a25317d1f3a9031"], "question": {"text": "If a wave gets refracted into a denser medium, then which of the following is true?"}, "options": [{"id": "c25543", "text": "Wavelength, speed and frequency decreases.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67fb"}, {"id": "87a0df", "text": "Wavelength increases, speed decreases and frequency remains constant.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67fc"}, {"id": "897ba4", "text": "Wavelength and speed decreases but frequency remains constant.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67fd"}, {"id": "399a8b", "text": "Wavelength, speed and frequency increases.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67fe"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f67ff", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["6162fb156ed13040ec84ade8"], "concepts": ["6162fb156ed13040ec84adc0"], "question": {"text": "A person standing on an open ground hears the sound of a jet aeroplane, coming from north at an angle <math><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> with ground level, but he finds the aeroplane right vertically above his position. If <math><mi>v</mi></math> is the speed of sound, speed of the plane is:"}, "options": [{"id": "70f2e9", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6800"}, {"id": "2392e1", "text": "<math><mi>v</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6801"}, {"id": "8affe3", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6802"}, {"id": "aa2ec1", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>v</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6803"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:10.326Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:10.326Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f684c"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6848", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f682c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f38"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4efb"], "question": {"text": "The percentage increase in the speed of transverse waves produced in a stretched string if the tension is increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></math>,&nbsp;will be ___ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "2c6315", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f682d"}, {"id": "a4a84c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f682e"}, {"id": "40f23c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f682f"}, {"id": "64e6a6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6830"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6831", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475b"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba0"], "question": {"text": "A one metre long (both ends open) organ pipe is kept in a gas that has double the density of air at STP. Assuming the speed of sound in air at STP is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the frequency difference between the fundamental and second harmonic of this pipe is __________ Hz."}, "options": [{"id": "47f1fc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6832"}, {"id": "72a41b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6833"}, {"id": "b8b898", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6834"}, {"id": "7344ec", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6835"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6836", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["6117b76e478ae845c43c6e13"], "concepts": ["6117b92b67dbe2603c3e945c"], "question": {"text": "A transverse harmonic wave on a string is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>003</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> are in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sec</mi></math>. The wave&nbsp;velocity is _________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "ee027e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6837"}, {"id": "001529", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6838"}, {"id": "36e243", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6839"}, {"id": "1207ad", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f683a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f683b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e56769499d1e49588f8f06"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c6304"], "question": {"text": "Two light beams of intensities <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi>I</mi></math> interfere on a screen. The phase difference between these beams on the screen at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is zero and at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi></math>. The difference of resultant intensities, at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>, will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "1be684", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f683c"}, {"id": "c83359", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f683d"}, {"id": "f44077", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f683e"}, {"id": "d88951", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f683f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6840", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e56769499d1e49588f8f08"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95cd"], "question": {"text": "A sonometer wire of resonating length $90 \\mathrm{~cm}$ has a fundamental frequency of $400 \\mathrm{~Hz}$ when kept under some tension. The resonating length of the wire with fundamental frequency of $600 \\mathrm{~Hz}$ under same tension _____$\\mathrm{cm}$."}, "options": [{"id": "4132c4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6841"}, {"id": "934192", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6842"}, {"id": "ec33e1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6843"}, {"id": "3a120f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efac677dc36a88f6844"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c